# Structure comes first

A material’s structure describes how its parts are arranged. Start with a small repeating pattern, then ask how that pattern shapes the object you can hold.

## A simple example

Compare a neat stack of blocks with a loose pile. Both use the same blocks, but their arrangements change how they respond to a push.

**Useful relationship:** ρ = m / V

## Pause and try

Sketch a repeating pattern. Identify one unit that can be repeated to reconstruct the whole sketch.

